From f256dadf24c046d31c14ae019b96b7df0ced775d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tina Odaka <tina.odaka@ifremer.fr>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 02:18:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add CRS-aware AffineSamplingGrid, the lossless +proj=healpix
 grid and GeoTIFF helpers
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

AffineSamplingGrid now follows the rasterio / GDAL conventions (the
transform maps pixel corners, the shape is (height, width)) and takes an
optional `crs`. Pixel centres of a projected grid are inverse-projected
before the cell lookup; pixels outside the projection's domain, and the
duplicate side of a seam, are masked instead of being passed to
healpix-geo (which panics on non-finite latitudes).

New:
- `healpix_plot.projection`: PROJ strings / pyproj CRSs for the ellipsoidal
  HEALPix projection built from healpix-geo's own ellipsoid parameters, and
  `cell_aligned_grid` (`AffineSamplingGrid.from_healpix`): the 45°-rotated
  grid in `+proj=healpix` with exactly one pixel per cell, so resampling
  onto it is lossless (level >= 1, lon_0 a multiple of 90°).
- `AffineSamplingGrid.from_raster`: the grid of a rasterio dataset or a
  rioxarray DataArray; `pixel_indices`: the pixel of each cell centre.
- `ConcreteSamplingGrid.lon / lat / valid / cell_ids / corners`.
- `healpix_plot.raster.to_dataarray`: a georeferenced xarray.DataArray
  (CRS + transform via rioxarray when available) ready for `.rio.to_raster`;
  `raster_cell_ids`: the cell id under every pixel of an existing raster.
- `healpix_plot.HEALPix`: a cartopy projection for `+proj=healpix` with the
  map outline, usable as `plot(..., projection="HEALPix")`.
- `plot` draws rotated grids with `pcolormesh` and projected grids in their
  own CRS.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
